/*!
\page page_stsvthit StSvtHit

\ref StSvtHit represents a single reconstructed space-point hit in the STAR Silicon Vertex
Tracker (SVT), a barrel silicon detector consisting of three concentric barrels (six layers)
arranged around the interaction region.  Each hit records the STAR global 3-D position (cm),
local sensor-frame coordinates in the anode and drift directions, the cluster's peak ADC value,
and the cluster's extent in anodes and time-buckets.

\see StSvtHitCollection

\section sec_svthit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StObject
└── StMeasuredPoint
    └── StHit
        └── StSvtHit
\endverbatim

Hits are collected in \ref StSvtHitCollection, organised as a four-level hierarchy:

\verbatim
StSvtHitCollection
└── StSvtBarrelHitCollection   (3 barrels)
    └── StSvtLadderHitCollection
        └── StSvtWaferHitCollection  (holds StSvtHit* via StSPtrVecSvtHit)
\endverbatim

\section sec_svthit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_svthit_inherited Inherited from StHit

- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Packed hardware address.  Bits 4–12 encode a flat hybrid
  index (0–431) identifying barrel, ladder, wafer, and hybrid.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-σ position errors in the STAR global frame (cm).
  <em>Not persisted.</em>
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Integrated cluster charge (ADC counts).
- <tt>Int_t mId</tt> — Cluster identifier.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — Geant track ID of the primary contributor (simulation only).
- <tt>UShort_t mQuality</tt> — Fraction of charge from <tt>mIdTruth</tt> (percent).
- <tt>UChar_t mFitFlag</tt> — Non-zero if used in a track fit.
- <tt>UChar_t mTrackRefCount</tt> — Number of tracks referencing this hit.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — Hit status flag bitmask.

\subsection subsec_svthit_own Own Data Members

- <tt>Float_t mPeak</tt> — Peak ADC value of the hit cluster.
- <tt>Float_t mAnode</tt> — Anode centroid position in units of ¼ anode pitch.
- <tt>Float_t mTimebucket</tt> — Drift-direction centroid position in units of ¼ time-bucket.
- <tt>Float_t mLocalPosition[2]</tt> — Local hit position (cm): [0] = anode direction, [1] = drift direction.
- <tt>UShort_t mNumberOfAnodes</tt> — Number of anode strips in the cluster.
- <tt>UShort_t mNumberOfPixels</tt> — Total pixels (anode × time-bucket) in the cluster.
- <tt>static StMemoryPool mPool</tt> — Per-class memory pool. <em>Not persisted.</em>

\section sec_svthit_geometry Geometry Decoding

The flat hybrid index in <tt>mHardwarePosition</tt> (bits 4–12) is the primary geometry key:

| Barrel | Active ladders | Hybrids/ladder | Wafers/ladder | Layer numbers |
|--------|---------------|----------------|---------------|---------------|
| 1      | 8             | 8              | 4             | 1 (even), 2 (odd) |
| 2      | 12            | 12             | 6             | 3 (even), 4 (odd) |
| 3      | 16            | 14             | 7             | 5 (even), 6 (odd) |

<b>volumeID</b> = <tt>10000 × shell + 1000 × layer + 100 × wafer + ladder</tt>.

\section sec_svthit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>unsigned int barrel() const</tt> — Barrel number (1–3).
- <tt>unsigned int ladder() const</tt> — Ladder number within the barrel.
- <tt>unsigned int wafer() const</tt> — Wafer number on the ladder.
- <tt>unsigned int hybrid() const</tt> — Hybrid number (1 or 2).
- <tt>unsigned int layer() const</tt> — SVT layer number (1–6).
- <tt>unsigned int shell() const</tt> — Shell: 1 = East, 2 = West.
- <tt>float anode() const</tt> — Anode centroid (¼ anode pitch).
- <tt>float timebucket() const</tt> — Drift centroid (¼ time-bucket).
- <tt>float peakADC() const</tt> — Peak ADC value.
- <tt>float localPosition(unsigned int i) const</tt> — Local position along axis <tt>i</tt> (cm).
- <tt>int numberOfAnodes() const</tt> — Cluster size in anodes.
- <tt>int numberOfPixels() const</tt> — Cluster size in pixels.
- <tt>virtual int volumeID() const</tt> — Packed geometry ID.
- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns <tt>kSvtId</tt>.

\section sec_svthit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StSvtHit uses a custom <tt>StMemoryPool</tt> allocator.  Once added to
\ref StSvtHitCollection, ownership belongs to the framework.
\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StSvtHit pointers obtained from the collection.

\section sec_svthit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StSvtHitCollection* svtColl = event->svtHitCollection();
if (!svtColl) return;

for (unsigned int iBarrel = 0; iBarrel < svtColl->numberOfBarrels(); ++iBarrel) {
    const StSvtBarrelHitCollection* barrel = svtColl->barrel(iBarrel);
    if (!barrel) continue;
    for (unsigned int iLadder = 0; iLadder < barrel->numberOfLadders(); ++iLadder) {
        const StSvtLadderHitCollection* ladder = barrel->ladder(iLadder);
        if (!ladder) continue;
        for (unsigned int iWafer = 0; iWafer < ladder->numberOfWafers(); ++iWafer) {
            const StSvtWaferHitCollection* wafer = ladder->wafer(iWafer);
            if (!wafer) continue;
            const StSPtrVecSvtHit& hits = wafer->hits();
            for (const StSvtHit* hit : hits) {
                float localAnode = hit->localPosition(0); // anode dir (cm)
                float localDrift = hit->localPosition(1); // drift dir (cm)
                unsigned int layer = hit->layer();        // 1–6
            }
        }
    }
}
\endcode

*/
